ok - session ids are scoped by firstmate home (the pipe namespace is machine-global)
ok - target parsing accepts one atom and refuses anything that could address another pipe
ok - host gate: running ON Windows, refusal path not applicable
ok - key vocabulary normalizes the spellings callers vary on and passes the rest through
ok - agent_state passes the daemon's full recovery vocabulary through unchanged
ok - an unrecognized state word degrades to unreadable, never to a recovery-licensing verdict
ok - with no state answer the durable record decides even though the client exits nonzero, and a contradictory live pipe stays unreadable
ok - a malformed target is unreadable, never dead
ok - the three-state view collapses only authoritative absence to dead
ok - busy state is a direct output-age measurement with an explicit unknown
ok - capability descriptor declares styled + true cursor (the first non-tmux backend able to)
ok - composer verdicts come from the shared classifier, cursor-anchored
ok - an unusable cursor row refuses loudly instead of classifying the wrong shape
ok - the composer is read in ONE client call, so the row and screen cannot straddle a redraw
ok - create_task refuses an existing live session before spawning anything
ok - create_task spawns a home-scoped shell session and confirms it answers before reporting success
ok - create_task refuses to arm a CR-bearing rcfile and spawns the session unarmed instead
ok - create_task does not offer --rcfile to a pinned non-bash session shell
ok - literal text is delivered by file, so no payload is exposed to Windows command-line quoting
ok - send_key normalizes then forwards
ok - capture forwards a numeric scrollback depth and sanitizes anything else
ok - list_live is scoped to this firstmate home and confirmed by a live ping, never by a stored pid
ok - a leftover session directory with no answering pipe is not reported live
ok - kill is best-effort and never forwards a target it could not parse
ok - a well-formed conpty endpoint validates and reports its backend and target
ok - a window that disagrees with conpty_session is refused, preserving task state
ok - an endpoint bound to another task is refused
ok - a conpty record with no session identifier is refused
ok - conpty is registered as a known, spawn-capable, explicitly-selected backend needing no JSON parser
ok - conpty liveness: the shell's prompt mark settles the foreground, and silence falls back instead of inferring dead
ok - conpty liveness: the marker tracker reads split marks, both terminators, ignores untagged ones, and resynchronises rather than letting a stale OSC swallow a mark
ok - conpty liveness: the fallback screen reading survives a sparse viewport and a prompt left in scrollback
ok - conpty liveness: a session whose process list cannot be read still reports its prompt-mark chain, so a transient poll failure is a retry rather than a dead end
ok - conpty shell integration: the armed shell marks both command start and the return to its prompt
ok - conpty shell integration: the command-start mark writes no stray control bytes onto the pty
ok - conpty shell integration: a nested shell continues the mark chain, and stops marking when the carriers are withheld
ok - conpty shell integration: a shell that cannot mark a running command marks no prompts either, so an inherited prompt hook can never report a live agent as stopped
ok - conpty shell integration: SHELL is repaired unless a real executable image stands behind it, so treehouse opens a shell it can actually start
ok - conpty shell integration: each carrier is armed idempotently, so a re-source heals a wiped one and duplicates nothing
ok - conpty shell integration: an operator's array-form prompt hooks survive arming without the trailing one running twice
ok - conpty shell integration: an operator's inline comment in one array hook does not swallow the hooks after it
ok - conpty shell integration: an operator's pre-set PS0 survives arming, and re-sourcing adds no second mark
ok - conpty shell integration: an operator's own prompt hook still reads the command's exit status through the mark hook, on both the zero and the non-zero arm
ok - conpty adapter unit tests complete
